<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title><%= title %></title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/global.css">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.0/css/all.min.css">
    <style>
        :root {
            --exam-primary: #0f766e;
            --exam-accent: #f59e0b;
            --exam-surface: #f8fafc;
            --exam-ink: #0f172a;
            --exam-muted: #475569;
            --exam-border: #dbe4ee;
        }

        body {
            background: radial-gradient(circle at top right, #e0f2fe 0%, #f8fafc 45%, #fefce8 100%);
            color: var(--exam-ink);
        }

        .external-header {
            position: sticky;
            top: 0;
            z-index: 20;
            backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
            background: rgba(248, 250, 252, 0.8);
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--exam-border);
        }

        .external-header .container {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
            padding-top: 1rem;
            padding-bottom: 1rem;
            gap: 1rem;
        }

        .brand {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0.6rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--exam-primary);
        }

        .brand i {
            font-size: 1.15rem;
        }

        .external-nav {
            display: flex;
            gap: 1rem;
            color: var(--exam-muted);
            font-weight: 500;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            justify-content: flex-end;
        }

        .external-nav a:hover {
            color: var(--exam-primary);
        }

        .hero {
            padding: 3.5rem 0 2rem;
        }

        .hero-card {
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
            border: 1px solid var(--exam-border);
            border-radius: 16px;
            padding: 2rem;
            box-shadow: 0 14px 30px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
        }

        .hero h1 {
            font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 3rem);
            line-height: 1.2;
            margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
        }

        .hero p {
            color: var(--exam-muted);
            max-width: 860px;
        }

        .pill-row {
            margin-top: 1.3rem;
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 0.65rem;
        }

        .pill {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0.45rem;
            padding: 0.45rem 0.85rem;
            border-radius: 999px;
            font-size: 0.88rem;
            border: 1px solid var(--exam-border);
            background: #ffffff;
            color: #0f172a;
        }

        .pill strong {
            color: var(--exam-primary);
        }

        .grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr);
            gap: 1rem;
            margin: 1.75rem 0 3rem;
        }

        .card {
            background: #ffffff;
            border: 1px solid var(--exam-border);
            border-radius: 14px;
            padding: 1.25rem;
            box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06);
        }

        .card h2 {
            font-size: 1.05rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
            color: var(--exam-primary);
        }

        .card p,
        .card li {
            color: var(--exam-muted);
        }

        .span-12 { grid-column: span 12; }
        .span-7 { grid-column: span 7; }
        .span-5 { grid-column: span 5; }
        .span-6 { grid-column: span 6; }

        .flow {
            display: grid;
            gap: 0.55rem;
            margin-top: 0.7rem;
        }

        .flow-step {
            border: 1px dashed #99c3e5;
            border-radius: 10px;
            padding: 0.75rem;
            background: #f8fbff;
            color: #1e3a5f;
            font-weight: 500;
        }

        .metric-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(140px, 1fr));
            gap: 0.7rem;
        }

        .metric {
            border: 1px solid var(--exam-border);
            border-radius: 10px;
            padding: 0.75rem;
            background: var(--exam-surface);
        }

        .metric .value {
            font-size: 1.25rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: #0f172a;
        }

        .metric .label {
            font-size: 0.84rem;
            color: var(--exam-muted);
        }

        .demo-script {
            border-left: 5px solid var(--exam-accent);
            background: #fffdf5;
        }

        .demo-script ol {
            margin-left: 1rem;
            display: grid;
            gap: 0.45rem;
        }

        .footer-note {
            margin: 2rem 0 2.75rem;
            color: var(--exam-muted);
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 0.95rem;
        }

        @media (max-width: 900px) {
            .span-7,
            .span-6,
            .span-5 {
                grid-column: span 12;
            }

            .external-header .container {
                flex-direction: column;
                align-items: flex-start;
            }

            .external-nav {
                justify-content: flex-start;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header class="external-header">
        <div class="container">
            <a href="/" class="brand">
                <i class="fas fa-gears"></i>
                <span>Mail Automation Engineering Brief</span>
            </a>
            <nav class="external-nav">
                <a href="/">Home</a>
                <% if (user) { %>
                    <a href="/<%= user.role %>/dashboard">Dashboard</a>
                <% } else { %>
                    <a href="/auth">Login</a>
                <% } %>
            </nav>
        </div>
    </header>

    <main class="container">
        <section class="hero" id="overview">
            <div class="hero-card">
                <h1>End-to-End AI Mail Pipeline (Built by Our Team)</h1>
                <p>
                    This page explains the engineering we implemented ourselves: email ingestion, feature extraction,
                    AI classification through OpenRouter, confidence scoring, human correction loop, and metrics tracking.
                    The orchestration tool helps with transport, but decision logic, auditability, and learning loop are our own.
                </p>

                <div class="pill-row">
                    <span class="pill"><i class="fas fa-robot"></i> Model Provider: <strong>OpenRouter</strong></span>
                    <span class="pill"><i class="fas fa-brain"></i> Model: <strong>acree-ai</strong></span>
                    <span class="pill"><i class="fas fa-shield-halved"></i> Guardrails: <strong>Rule + confidence checks</strong></span>
                    <span class="pill"><i class="fas fa-chart-line"></i> Learning: <strong>Human feedback loop</strong></span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="grid" id="pipeline">
            <article class="card span-7">
                <h2><i class="fas fa-diagram-project"></i> Processing Flow</h2>
                <p>The classifier is intentionally explainable so each prediction can be audited during review.</p>
                <div class="flow">
                    <div class="flow-step">1) Ingest email from webhook and normalize sender, subject, body, attachments.</div>
                    <div class="flow-step">2) Extract engineered signals (keywords, urgency, reply intent, job markers).</div>
                    <div class="flow-step">3) Send structured prompt to OpenRouter <code>acree-ai</code> for category prediction.</div>
                    <div class="flow-step">4) Compute confidence and attach top reasons behind classification.</div>
                    <div class="flow-step">5) Route high-confidence emails automatically; queue low-confidence for admin review.</div>
                    <div class="flow-step">6) Capture admin corrections and feed them back into weights/prompts.</div>
                </div>
            </article>

            <article class="card span-5">
                <h2><i class="fas fa-tags"></i> Category Output</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Job Opportunities</li>
                    <li>Internships</li>
                    <li>Reply from Company</li>
                    <li>Competitions</li>
                    <li>Urgent</li>
                    <li>Uncategorized (fallback)</li>
                </ul>
            </article>

            <article class="card span-6" id="engineering">
                <h2><i class="fas fa-screwdriver-wrench"></i> Engineering Contributions</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Custom prompt contract and strict JSON response parsing for deterministic downstream usage.</li>
                    <li>Confidence thresholding to separate auto-routing vs. manual review workload.</li>
                    <li>Explainability payload with machine-readable reasons for each prediction.</li>
                    <li>Fallback behavior if model/API fails: safe default category and review queue.</li>
                    <li>Correction logging to improve future runs with updated patterns and prompt examples.</li>
                </ul>
            </article>

            <article class="card span-6" id="metrics">
                <h2><i class="fas fa-gauge-high"></i> MVP Success Metrics</h2>
                <div class="metric-grid">
                    <div class="metric">
                        <div class="value">Accuracy</div>
                        <div class="label">Category-level prediction correctness</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="metric">
                        <div class="value">Precision/Recall</div>
                        <div class="label">Per-category quality score</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="metric">
                        <div class="value">Review Load</div>
                        <div class="label">Low-confidence queue size</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="metric">
                        <div class="value">Time Saved</div>
                        <div class="label">Manual triage minutes reduced</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </article>

            <article class="card span-12 demo-script" id="demo">
                <h2><i class="fas fa-chalkboard-user"></i> External Examiner Demo Script</h2>
                <ol>
                    <li>Show one raw email arriving in the system (subject/body/attachments).</li>
                    <li>Open predicted category, confidence score, and top reasons returned by model.</li>
                    <li>Manually correct one wrong category to prove reviewer-in-the-loop design.</li>
                    <li>Show that the correction is stored for future prompt/weight improvements.</li>
                    <li>Display dashboard metrics to quantify engineering impact over time.</li>
                </ol>
            </article>
        </section>

        <p class="footer-note">
            Suggested env variables for this flow: <code>OPENROUTER_API_KEY</code>, <code>OPENROUTER_MODEL=acree-ai</code>,
            <code>N8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code>. Keep secrets server-side and never expose them in client code.
        </p>
    </main>
</body>
</html>
